{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr48a5ra7bz","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"EWM live pass-rate scores only single step in level transitions","summary":"The EWM agent's live pass-rate (used to drop a mispredicting world-model program to reactive) must only score SINGLE-action observed transitions that do NOT cross a level boundary. The suite records a multi-action plan batch as ONE grid-in/grid-out transition keyed on the first action, and a level-transition after-grid is the NEXT level's initial frame (often a different shape) — neither has a well-defined one-step model prediction, so scoring them falsely penalizes a correct model (observed: smoke live_pass_rate 0.0 for a correct program until these were excluded). Gate the live-window append on len(executed)<=1 and stop_reason != 'level_transition'.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T01:01:48.838Z","vec":[0.00667130621150136,0.02140769548714161,-0.030684413388371468,0.08756185322999954,0.1113402247428894,0.01854703761637211,-0.07333267480134964,0.0024934459943324327,-0.04339221864938736,-0.003976003732532263,0.013828592374920845,-0.07360643148422241,0.0053728739731013775,-0.017933398485183716,0.06300413608551025,0.041866809129714966,-0.02168915420770645,-0.0826730877161026,-0.04325210675597191,-0.07560186833143234,-0.008333241567015648,-0.033728331327438354,0.04008226469159126,0.014645746909081936,-0.049821458756923676,-0.02801848202943802,-0.07366976886987686,0.060649145394563675,0.0711115375161171,-0.03777076676487923,0.068721242249012,0.029893208295106888,-0.07517777383327484,0.02604304999113083,-0.02021442912518978,-0.023066844791173935,-0.023767462000250816,-0.05762225389480591,-0.041479937732219696,-0.014236003160476685,0.0873609408736229,0.00738515192642808,-0.025772137567400932,-0.017078878358006477,0.037175342440605164,0.014952180907130241,-0.05996868014335632,-0.02436031587421894,-0.0933104157447815,0.026195984333753586,-0.011341354809701443,0.01735